     "DefaultGraphicsInteraction" -> {
      "Version" -> 1.2, "TrackMousePosition" -> {True, False}, 
       "Effects" -> {
        "Highlight" -> {"ratio" -> 2}, "HighlightPoint" -> {"ratio" -> 2}, 
         "Droplines" -> {
          "freeformCursorMode" -> True, 
           "placement" -> {"x" -> "All", "y" -> "None"}}}}, "RotationControl" -> 
     "Globe"},
   PlotRange->{{-4, 6}, {-3, 7}, {-25., 84.99998142857245}},
   PlotRangePadding->{
     Scaled[0.02], 
     Scaled[0.02], 
     Scaled[0.02]},
   Ticks->{Automatic, Automatic, Automatic},
   ViewPoint->{3.1188114096586284`, -1.2928855876524952`, 
    0.22685292200813492`},
   ViewVertical->{-0.0619307269245983, 0.025673031727949023`, 
    0.9977502094735369}]], "Output",
  CellChangeTimes->{3.9396462538751907`*^9, 3.93995601529775*^9, 
   3.9399560566728287`*^9},ExpressionUUID->
  "31288433-4ac8-438c-98e4-ffc35b703566"],
 "\nEl plano tangente, cerca del punto de tangencia, puede ser una buena \
aproximaci\[OAcute]n de la funci\[OAcute]n y puede ser m\[AAcute]s \
f\[AAcute]cil evaluar el plano (un polinomio) que la funci\[OAcute]n.\n\nPor \
ejemplo, si ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["e", 
     RowBox[{"x", "+", 
      RowBox[{"2", "y"}]}]]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1950140e-8581-4330-a89a-ade022b11975"],
 ", el plano tangente en el punto (0,0) es\n\t\tz=f(0,0) + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0219ac4e-9f88-4697-9f5c-f709744df6d8"],
 " (x-0)+",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "y"], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0bc4b378-b98b-4cab-99cc-a24770a0031d"],
 " (y-0) = 1+1*x+2*y = 1+x+2y\nAs\[IAcute] f(x,y)\[TildeEqual]1+x+2y \
alrededor del (0,0).\n\nPor ejemplo, f(0.1,0.1) = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", 
    RowBox[{"0.1", "+", 
     RowBox[{"2", "*", "0.1"}]}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c88eb3df-f23c-4320-9851-5c779972d8e1"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", "0.2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "33797204-f2ba-4085-8350-2ef909a0891b"],
 " = 1.34986... mientras que el plano tangente vale 1+0.1+2*0.1=1.3.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Estimaci\[OAcute]n de errores",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\nEn la pr\[AAcute]ctica, los datos experimentales est\[AAcute]n sometidos \
a errores y las funciones que evaluamos con esos datos tendr\[AAcute]n \
errores. Una forma de estimar los errores que los datos pueden inducir en una \
funci\[OAcute]n es usar el plano tangente y tener una estimaci\[OAcute]n del \
error. \n\tError en la funci\[OAcute]n f = |f(x,y)-f(x0,y0)| \[TildeEqual] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"|", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
     RowBox[{"f", "(", 
      RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "|"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"baea16d6-aad5-4880-9510-b50e68656a08"],
 " * (error en la x) + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"|", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "y"], 
     RowBox[{"f", "(", 
      RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "|"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"99400bc1-537c-435e-a464-f9a76ef30ad5"],
 "* (error en la y).\n\nCon el error que puede haber en las variables x e y, \
los multiplicamos por las derivadas parciales en el punto medido y sumamos \
para obtener una estimaci\[OAcute]n del error m\[AAcute]ximo que \
podr\[IAcute]amos tener en la funci\[OAcute]n.\n\n",
 StyleBox["C\[AAcute]lculo de extremos relativos.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\nEn una variable utiliz\[AAcute]bamos la derivada para calcular los \
extremos relativos (m\[AAcute]ximos y m\[IAcute]nimos) de una \
funci\[OAcute]n. La idea era que si una funci\[OAcute]n derivable \
ten\[IAcute]a un m\[AAcute]ximo relativo (o un m\[IAcute]nimo relativo) en un \
punto interior al dominio, su derivada deb\[IAcute]a ser cero. \nEn dos \
variables, si una funci\[OAcute]n tiene un m\[AAcute]ximo o m\[IAcute]nimo \
relativo en (x0,y0), punto interior del dominio, tendremos que ser\[AAcute] m\
\[AAcute]ximo o m\[IAcute]nimo relativo en los puntos de la forma (x,y0) \
\[OAcute] (x0,y), por tanto las derivadas parciales ser\[AAcute]n cero. \nAs\
\[IAcute], cuando queramos buscar extremos relativos resolveremos el sistema\n\
\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f8a2a726-258b-45b8-9393-8fce73651333"],
 " = 0\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "y"], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0d16c52c-52e8-46c2-9bd5-8401af807132"],
 " = 0\nLas soluciones del sistema nos pueden llevar a los m\[AAcute]ximos y \
m\[IAcute]nimos relativos.\n\nNos obstante, aparecen nuevas situaciones. As\
\[IAcute], la funci\[OAcute]n f(x,y) =  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b8fea0e9-b708-4b17-a407-2a583473ab3b"],
 " - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8b92c5d4-2c91-4f2f-9493-40882ad52847"],
 ", en los puntos (x,0), f(x,0) = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2f46661c-6e28-4359-b621-fe2363a8065c"],
 " y tendr\[AAcute] un m\[IAcute]nimo en el (0,0), en cambio en los puntos \
(0,y), f(0,y) =  - ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0656782d-f5ef-4f70-8f0c-880c58640526"],
 ", con lo que en el (0,0) habr\[IAcute]a un m\[AAcute]ximo en esta direcci\
\[OAcute]n. Diremos que f(x,y) tiene un ",
 StyleBox["punto de silla",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " en el (0,0).\n\nPara saber si un punto donde se anulan las derivadas es m\
\[AAcute]ximo, m\[IAcute]nimo o punto de silla, recurrimos a las derivadas \
segundas. La situaci\[OAcute]n es similar a lo que ocurre en una variable (si \
la derivada segunda era positiva hab\[IAcute]a un m\[IAcute]nimo, si la \
derivada segunda era negativa hab\[IAcute]a un m\[AAcute]ximo y si la \
derivada segunda era cero, aparec\[IAcute]a un caso de duda). \n\nAhora hay \
cuatro derivadas segundas:\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], 
        RowBox[{"f", "(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}]},
      {
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
          RowBox[{"y", ",", "y"}]], "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}]}
     }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "07c61981-5d8d-4ed7-a3ec-9fbb451cf79d"],
 " es la matriz hessiana\nEl determinante de esta matriz es el hessiano:\n\t\t\
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"|", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], 
        RowBox[{"f", "(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}]},
      {
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
          RowBox[{"y", ",", "y"}]], "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}]}
     }], "|"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "edc54f64-6652-4749-8032-c1bd00512d80"],
 "\nSi al resolver el sistema\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "758781bf-23b3-4857-8801-09bc31e5e958"],
 " = 0\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "y"], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "facf7ecb-fa4f-4bc3-9be4-8cbc0dadf9e0"],
 " = 0\nnos encontramos con un punto (x0,y0) donde se anulan las primeras \
derivadas parciales, pasamos a calcular el Hessiano en ese punto\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\t\t", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Hessiano", "(", 
      RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}], "=", 
     RowBox[{"|", GridBox[{
        {
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], 
          RowBox[{"f", "(", 
           RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], 
          RowBox[{"f", "(", 
           RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}]},
        {
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], 
          RowBox[{"f", "(", 
           RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], 
         RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
           RowBox[{"y", ",", "y"}]], 
          RowBox[{"f", "(", 
           RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}]}
       }], "|"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cce662fe-f1a4-4d91-825e-f051c28e74c9"],
 ".\n* Si el Hessiano en ese punto es negativo, tendremos un punto de silla. \
\n* Si el Hessiano es positivo, habr\[AAcute] un m\[AAcute]ximo o un m\
\[IAcute]nimo. Para saber si es m\[AAcute]ximo o m\[IAcute]nimo, debemos \
estudiar la derivada segunda (en la x o la y, da igual). Si la derivada \
segunda ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ea9c1654-7279-42dd-8833-a798f75e7f49"],
 " es mayor que cero, habr\[AAcute] un m\[IAcute]nimo, si la derivada segunda \
fuese negativa, tendr\[IAcute]amos un m\[AAcute]ximo.\n* Si el Hessiano es \
cero, tendr\[IAcute]amos un caso de duda y deber\[IAcute]amos estudiarlo por \
otros m\[EAcute]todos.\n\n",
 StyleBox["C\[AAcute]lculo de m\[AAcute]ximos y m\[IAcute]nimos absolutos",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\nComo ocurr\[IAcute]a en una variable, en ocasiones nos interesa conocer, \
si existen, los m\[AAcute]ximos y m\[IAcute]nimos absolutos. En muchas \
ocasiones, los m\[AAcute]ximos o m\[IAcute]nimos absolutos no existen. El \
Teorema de Weierstrass nos garantiza, bajo unas hip\[OAcute]tesis sencillas, \
que existe m\[AAcute]ximo y m\[IAcute]nimo absolutos. En concreto, dice que \
si una funci\[OAcute]n es continua en un conjunto cerrado y acotado, alcanza \
su m\[AAcute]ximo y m\[IAcute]nimo absolutos.\n\nEn una variable, cuando ten\
\[IAcute]amos una funci\[OAcute]n continua en un intervalo [a,b], \
ten\[IAcute]amos garantizada la existencia de m\[AAcute]ximo y m\[IAcute]nimo \
absolutos. Para encontrarlos, consider\[AAcute]bamos los puntos extremos y \
los puntos del interior. En el interior, consider\[AAcute]bamos los puntos \
con derivada cero y los puntos sin derivada. Con todos los puntos \
encontrados, evaluamos la funci\[OAcute]n en esos puntos y encontramos d\
\[OAcute]nde esta el m\[AAcute]ximo y el m\[IAcute]nimo de la \
funci\[OAcute]n.\n\nEn varias variables, si tenemos una funci\[OAcute]n \
continua en un conjunto cerrado y acotado, tendremos m\[AAcute]ximo y m\
\[IAcute]nimo absolutos, que podr\[AAcute]n estar en el borde o en el \
interior. Cuando la funci\[OAcute]n es derivable, los puntos candidatos del \
interior ser\[AAcute]n los que tengan primera derivada cero. El problema \
aparece en el borde, pues no son solo dos puntos como en los intervalos de \
una variable, ahora aparecen infinitos.\nEn ocasiones podremos despejar una \
variable en funci\[OAcute]n de la otra y dejar la funci\[OAcute]n en una \
\[UAcute]nica variable. Otras veces, podremos expresar los puntos del borde \
en t\[EAcute]rminos de un par\[AAcute]metro y llegar a una funci\[OAcute]n de \
una variable. Otra opci\[OAcute]n es la t\[EAcute]cnica de los \
Multiplicadores de Lagrange.\n\nSupongamos que los puntos del borde son los \
que cumplen g(x,y)=0. Para calcular los m\[AAcute]ximos y m\[IAcute]nimos \
absolutos de f(x,y) con la condici\[OAcute]n g(x,y)=0, construimos la funci\
\[OAcute]n:\n\t\tF(x,y,t) = f(x,y) + t g(x,y) \ny buscamos las soluciones del \
sistema\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "x"], 
    RowBox[{"F", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "t"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"bc7f656d-2bcb-4dbe-b3fb-32a4332aee25"],
 " = 0\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "y"], 
    RowBox[{"F", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "t"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"4f454559-0002-4087-bce7-d852defae008"],
 " = 0\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"F", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "t"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"aa52b7ee-5c6e-4844-8492-94c7c2300d14"],
 " = 0\nLos valores soluci\[OAcute]n de x e y, ser\[AAcute]n candidatos a m\
\[AAcute]ximos y m\[IAcute]nimos.\nObservemos que la condici\[OAcute]n ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "t"], 
    RowBox[{"F", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x", ",", "y", ",", "t"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"877d437b-7d0a-4bc4-a00d-202d3d488659"],
 " =0 es equivalente a g(x,y)=0.\n\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7240604714667296`*^9, 3.72406048662873*^9}, {
   3.7240610587387295`*^9, 3.7240611018827295`*^9}, {3.939954958647408*^9, 
   3.9399551721279755`*^9}, 3.939955527846342*^9, {3.939955571831538*^9, 
   3.9399556523583617`*^9}, {3.9399556840014973`*^9, 
   3.9399556874621887`*^9}, {3.9399557413454447`*^9, 3.939955835502502*^9}, {
   3.939955873271575*^9, 3.9399559214736443`*^9}, {3.9399560967031803`*^9, 
   3.939956174345827*^9}, {3.9399562160471725`*^9, 3.9399564877470765`*^9}, {
   3.939956533616193*^9, 3.9399566342101765`*^9}, {3.9399566779724913`*^9, 
   3.9399569254625883`*^9}, {3.9399569707710896`*^9, 
   3.9399569761850777`*^9}, {3.9399570127278275`*^9, 3.93995713381279*^9}, {
   3.939957202909025*^9, 3.9399572838750787`*^9}, {3.939958978573118*^9, 
   3.9399592325063887`*^9}, {3.9399592873834987`*^9, 
   3.9399593106740465`*^9}, {3.939959381572998*^9, 3.9399594777474527`*^9}, {
   3.9399595122152643`*^9, 3.9399597247210293`*^9}, {3.9399597738541713`*^9, 
   3.939959838880402*^9}, {3.9399598756639442`*^9, 3.9399601652902036`*^9}, {
   3.939965319500732*^9, 3.9399656897234144`*^9}, {3.939965724697365*^9, 
   3.939966057819022*^9}, {3.9399661228539743`*^9, 3.939966145897211*^9}, {
   3.93996618191619*^9, 3.939966190853273*^9}, {3.9399662548596992`*^9, 
   3.9399662663602486`*^9}, {3.939966306593867*^9, 3.939966324042761*^9}, {
   3.939966464873871*^9, 3.9399665680692735`*^9}, {3.939966606619549*^9, 
   3.9399666386439085`*^9}, {3.9399667385443144`*^9, 
   3.9399668901919446`*^9}, {3.9399670084160748`*^9, 
   3.9399670237218237`*^9}, {3.9399670630729904`*^9, 
   3.9399670831139517`*^9}, {3.939967171591609*^9, 3.9399672803359337`*^9}, {
   3.939967335730592*^9, 
   3.9399675042129927`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0c97b8b1-8262-4e7c-8aee-\
83e63396c25e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Derivadas", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9399657171943874`*^9, 3.9399657197618446`*^9}, {
  3.9399878028100214`*^9, 
  3.9399878139359674`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d15be6a0-65d6-4ad5-9937-\
8d9bf1de0345"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Como vimos al estudiar las funciones de una variable, la derivada es una \
herramienta para estudiar el cambio de una funci\[OAcute]n.\n\n",
 StyleBox["Derivada direccional.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\nTomando un vector unitario, v=(v1,v2), con m\[OAcute]dulo o longitud 1 \
(puede escribirse tambi\[EAcute]n de la forma (cos \[Theta], sen \[Theta]) ), \
podemos estudiar el cambio en un punto (x0,y0) en la direcci\[OAcute]n v \
comparando f((x0,y0)+t(v1,v2)) con f(x0,y0)\n\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"f", "(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"t", "(", 
        RowBox[{"v1", ",", "v2"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"f", "(", 
      RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "t"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"701d7a7f-3bc6-4cf3-89d1-1ada5c72b87d"],
 "\n\nSi existe el l\[IAcute]mite cuando t tiende a 0, diremos que existe la \
derivada de f en la direcci\[OAcute]n v, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["D", "v"], 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "02e3c264-151e-4e60-8e8b-d8bbd247c5c2"],
 ".\n\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["lim", 
      RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f", "(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"t", "(", 
          RowBox[{"v1", ",", "v2"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"f", "(", 
        RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "t"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["D", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"v1", ",", "v2"}], ")"}]], 
     RowBox[{"f", "(", 
      RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "08b21c2b-637e-4f56-a4cb-9c84cab0b151"],
 "\nSi el vector v es (1,0) hablamos de la ",
 StyleBox["derivada parcial respecto a la primera variable",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ":\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["lim", 
      RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f", "(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x0", "+", "t"}], ",", "y0"}], ")"}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"f", "(", 
        RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "t"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["D", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], ")"}]], 
      RowBox[{"f", "(", 
       RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"4254ba26-367b-4a62-b174-9b032c8c3751"],
 "\n\nAn\[AAcute]logamente, con el vector (0,1), llegar\[IAcute]amos a la ",
 StyleBox["derivada parcial respecto a la segunda variable",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ":\n\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["lim", 
      RowBox[{"t", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"f", "(", 
        RowBox[{"x0", ",", 
         RowBox[{"y0", "+", "t"}]}], ")"}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"f", "(", 
        RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "t"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["D", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ")"}]], 
      RowBox[{"f", "(", 
       RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"x0", ",", "y0"}], ")"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"b211312a-52b6-4dd2-9762-ddbdbeaf55e5"],
 "\n\nHabitualmente, para calcular las derivadas parciales no es necesario \
calcular estos l\[IAcute]mites. Basta recordar las reglas y propiedades de \
derivaci\[OAcute]n en una variable.\n\nAs\[IAcute], si ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"f", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], ")"}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"3", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "y"}], "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SuperscriptBox["y", "3"]}], "+", "xy", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"4", "y"}], "+", " ", "6"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "03443e2c-cf87-45d2-b7df-23c7acc9e952"],
 ", \n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"6", "xy"}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5cf85d1d-ae00-42be-888e-7338dc9f8b4d"],
 " + y,\n\t\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"3", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"6", 
      SuperscriptBox["y", "2"]}], "+", "x", "+", " ", "4"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"ece69f7e-761c-463c-9ee2-68894759d9f6"],
 "\nPodr\[IAcute]amos volver a derivar estas derivadas parciales,\n\t",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "2"], "f"}], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}], ")"}], "2"]], "=", 
     RowBox[{"6", "y"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4e32ecbf-ac96-4ae3-bcb1-e65a1c20777b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "2"], "f"}], 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]}]], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"6", "x"}], "+", "1"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "54cc8720-ccad-4cf2-a604-cf69e17ace19"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "2"], "f"}], 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}], 
       RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]}]], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"6", "x"}], "+", "1"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "af3a5eb3-9fef-41a5-9054-2eb9ae0fb3e5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "f"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "2"], "f"}], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}], ")"}], "2"]], "=", 
     RowBox[{"12", "y"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1eb3f35a-8996-4585-8f49-c7c7b33b34b7"],
 "\n\nObservamos que las derivadas parciales, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "2"], "f"}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}]}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "87af628c-e2db-416d-aa06-4ef664556071"],
 " y ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "2"], "f"}], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "x"}], 
     RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "y"}]}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9dc0f820-7e3d-46ad-8b60-c9ee02d479e0"],
 " son iguales. Esto es lo habitual. Puede demostrarse que ",
 StyleBox["si las derivadas parciales existen y son continuas, el orden de \
derivaci\[OAcute]n no importa.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " El Mathematica solo pide cu\[AAcute]ntas veces hay que derivar respecto a \
cada variable, sin pedir el orden de derivaci\[OAcute]n.\nPara calcular las \
derivadas de una funci\[OAcute]n de varias variables podemos usar la \
instrucci\[OAcute]n D y tambi\[EAcute]n la paleta."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7240604714667296`*^9, 3.72406048662873*^9}, {
   3.7240610587387295`*^9, 3.7240611018827295`*^9}, 
   3.9399877911771135`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"ecc306d9-2f66-4298-b20f-\
2ebedde3e3c0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x_", ",", "y_", ",", "z_"}], "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"3", 
    RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "y"}], " ", "+", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
    RowBox[{"y", "*", "z"}], "]"}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "x", "]"}], "*", 
    RowBox[{"y", "^", "2"}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.845902082415206*^9, 3.845902161689206*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0d49a27d-c6ce-4c4a-94df-95b1b3357883"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"g", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x_", ",", "y_"}], "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"y", "^", "2"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.845902173276206*^9, 3.8459021836222057`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8744188a-9adb-431c-8cd6-aaab6450fcd8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "La derivada direccional de la funci\[OAcute]n g en el punto (2,1) en la \
direcci\[OAcute]n (cos ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    FractionBox["\[Pi]", "6"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "53e5d16e-af89-430b-ab5d-7877579325c5"],
 ", sen ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    FractionBox["\[Pi]", "6"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "98a6eb0c-1edc-4781-ad5c-6e85279f93b7"],
 ") es:"
}], "Text",
