Cell["\<\
El \[IAcute]ndice de masa corporal calculado es 27.6817. La b\[AAcute]scula \
puede introducir un error de 0.346021, mientras que la cinta m\[EAcute]trica \
podr\[IAcute]a introducir un error de 0.651333. Por tanto, la cinta \
m\[EAcute]trica induce un error mayor (ser\[IAcute]a lo m\[AAcute]s urgente \
en cambiar). La estimaci\[OAcute]n del error debido a los datos \
err\[OAcute]neos puede llegar a 0.346021+0.651333=0.997354.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.724167324813321*^9, 
  3.7241675195243216`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8d80e7c7-9fcd-4a3e-a287-\
0ce68b844c43"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\

\tC\[AAcute]lculo de m\[AAcute]ximos y de m\[IAcute]nimos (y de puntos de \
silla). Extremos relativos
\t\
\>", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.500751345359375*^9, 3.500751379984375*^9}, {
  3.500790035609375*^9, 3.500790048953125*^9}, {3.569509423875*^9, 
  3.56950942659375*^9}, {3.570537368580125*^9, 3.57053737997075*^9}, {
  3.599199111625*^9, 3.5991991196875*^9}, {3.7240484327935295`*^9, 
  3.7240485112145295`*^9}, {3.7240485580755296`*^9, 3.7240485842175293`*^9}, {
  3.7240486164895296`*^9, 3.7240486419275293`*^9}, {3.7240486787515297`*^9, 
  3.7240487439725294`*^9}, {3.7240487740165296`*^9, 3.7240488171255293`*^9}, {
  3.7240622066157293`*^9, 3.7240622479027295`*^9}, {3.7241654583243213`*^9, 
  3.724165462428321*^9}, {3.724165517815321*^9, 3.724165518259321*^9}, {
  3.845902396367206*^9, 3.8459024271292057`*^9}},
 FontFamily->"Arial",
 FontSize->14,
 FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0.25098039215686274`, 0.5019607843137255],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.807843137254902, 0.9058823529411765, 
   1.],ExpressionUUID->"9d8b9d48-8045-4c7b-ba7f-a15767143af1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Al igual que con funciones de una variable, podemos preguntarnos por los m\
\[AAcute]ximos y m\[IAcute]nimos de una funci\[OAcute]n de varias variables.\n\
\nUna posibilidad es buscar m\[AAcute]ximos o m\[IAcute]nimos locales. Se \
trata de puntos donde la funci\[OAcute]n es mayor o igual (o menor o igual) \
que en todos los de un entorno del punto. Como las funciones suelen ser \
derivables, la herramienta que se utiliza en este caso es la derivada. Los \
puntos interiores del dominio de una funci\[OAcute]n derivable que sean m\
\[AAcute]ximos o m\[IAcute]nimos locales, lo ser\[AAcute]n en cada una de las \
variables, por tanto tendr\[AAcute]n todas las derivadas igual a cero. Por \
ello, derivamos y buscamos los posibles puntos.\n\nOtra posibilidad es buscar \
m\[AAcute]ximos o m\[IAcute]nimos absolutos en conjuntos cerrados y acotados. \
En esta situaci\[OAcute]n, basta que la funci\[OAcute]n sea continua para \
tener la seguridad de que existir\[AAcute]n (Teorema de Weiertrass). Para \
encontrarlos, distinguimos los puntos del interior y el borde. En el interior \
estar\[IAcute]an en puntos donde la derivada se anule, o en puntos donde la \
funci\[OAcute]n no sea derivable.\n\nConsideremos las funciones f1(x,y) = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "505d90dd-8957-4aed-9424-99ed279a903f"],
 "+ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a417a680-5d2a-458e-9bbd-e731127a6af6"],
 ", f2(x,y) = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "acecfd0b-6c58-403f-bd03-e22e8786251c"],
 "- ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "334e6c35-1cf7-422b-9dd4-972ae1347a39"],
 ", f3(x,y) = -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "67add634-7887-4218-9891-abccf0e0a901"],
 "- ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "69075270-e525-4557-87b6-501bbf5fe887"],
 ", f4(x,y) = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "4"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "82c130da-b07b-439c-8530-e911afca907f"],
 "+ ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["y", "4"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "67e58d27-9647-4a26-ae3f-17d6a97adff9"],
 ", y busquemos sus extremos relativos."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7240613714397297`*^9, 3.7240613756157293`*^9}, {
  3.7240614187487297`*^9, 3.7240614680987296`*^9}, {3.72406157050873*^9, 
  3.7240615830137296`*^9}, {3.7240769011318073`*^9, 3.724076940833807*^9}, {
  3.7240770182098074`*^9, 3.7240772967478094`*^9}, {3.72407738298461*^9, 
  3.7240773859018097`*^9}, {3.7240774339498105`*^9, 3.724077683191012*^9}, {
  3.724078291591816*^9, 3.724078324367416*^9}, {3.7241655102173214`*^9, 
  3.724165510709321*^9}, {3.845901857492206*^9, 3.845901858685206*^9}, {
  3.879159111936799*^9, 
  3.8791591390856004`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8a7bab68-db70-4816-8a55-\
e453c871ddb3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
   RowBox[{"x_", ",", "y_"}], "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["x", "2"], "+", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["y", "2"]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7240776856090117`*^9, 
  3.724077710366212*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c0e66331-3ed9-420b-b10b-\
76f5092a37d5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"D", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}], ",", "x"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", "0"}],
      ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"D", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}], ",", "y"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
      "0"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7240777168090124`*^9, 
  3.7240777479466124`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0c3c9f9a-7aac-479d-a448-\
01ca11723b81"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"y", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.7240777497250123`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"90a5f218-dddf-419f-bb74-\
1b3427bd5a0d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
El punto (0,0) es un punto cr\[IAcute]tico (candidato a ser m\[AAcute]ximo, m\
\[IAcute]nimo o punto de silla). Intentamos averiguarlo calculando el \
hessiano de la funci\[OAcute]n en el punto (0,0) \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7240778964274135`*^9, 
  3.724077957501414*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9bdc45f1-c513-4663-9afe-\
8761124e2414"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
   RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "x"}]], 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}]}]},
      {
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}]], 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         RowBox[{"y", ",", "y"}]], 
        RowBox[{"f1", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", "y"}], "]"}]}]}
     }], ")"}], "]"}], "/.", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"x", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"y", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7240777831714125`*^9, 3.7240777913926125`*^9}, {
  3.724077829441013*^9, 
  3.724077883479413*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f0be12c6-9cf2-435f-a008-\
51fdc0cebdec"],

Cell[BoxData["4"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.7240778854762135`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"6dddb705-07de-4a4d-a545-\
ab0dbdc11194"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
